00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.030 align:start position:0%
 
good afternoon  the covet pandemic remains a severe  threat  to people's health and to people's  livelihood we are  in a race against time the faster we  reach  our target of having 70 percent of the  adult population  in europe vaccinated the better the  chances we have  of containing the virus and the good  news  is vaccination is picking up speed  across europe  member states have received over 126  million doses of vaccines  as of yesterday and i'm happy to say  that today we have reached the 100  million vaccinations  in the european union this is a  milestone that we can be proud of  of these 100 million vaccinations  more than a quarter already second doses  that means that we have now more than 27  million  europeans fully vaccinated and this is  good news  but as we can see with the announcement  by johnson and johnson yesterday  there are still many factors that can  disrupt the planned delivery schedules  of vaccines  it is therefore important to act swiftly  anticipate and adjust whenever it is  possible  and we are doing everything in our power  to support  europe's vaccination rollout also by  increasing the supply of vaccines in the  coming weeks and months  and this is why i'm pleased to announce  that we have reached an agreement with  biontech pfizer  to once again speed up the delivery of  vaccines  50 million additional doses of biotech  pfizer vaccines  will be delivered in quarter two  beginning in april  those 50 million doses were initially  foreseen for delivery  um in the fourth quarter of 2021  now they are available in the second  quarter  of 2021 that is right now  and this will bring the total doses  delivered by biontech pfizer  to 250 million doses in the second  quarter  these doses will be distributed the 50  million doses that we have now  additionally will be distributed  pro rata population among the member  states  and i think this will substantially help  consolidate the rollout of our  vaccination campaigns  i want to thank biontech pfizer it has  proven to be a reliable partner  it has delivered on its commitments and  it is responsive to our needs  and this is to the immediate benefit of  the eu  citizens and population but let me  also focus on the medium term  to prepare for the future we are drawing  the lessons  from the first phase of our answer to  the pandemic  it is clear that to defeat the virus  decisively  we will need to be prepared for the  following  at a certain point in time we might need  booster jobs to reinforce and prolong  immunity  and if an escape variant occurs  we will need to develop vaccines that  are adapted  to the new escape variant and we will  need them early  in sufficient quantities and having all  this in mind and having learned the  lessons  in this pandemic we need to focus  now on technologies that have proven  their worth  mrna vaccines are a clear case  in point and based on all this  we are now entering into a negotiations  with biontech pfizer for a third  contract  this contract will foresee the delivery  of 1.8 billion  additional doses of vaccine over the  period of 2022  and 2023  and it will entail not only the  production of vaccines  but also the essential components all of  that will be  based in the european union  the negotiations we are launching today  and i hope to conclude them  very rapidly our further important step  in europe's response to the pandemic  other contracts with  other companies may follow we are in  this together  and we will win this fight against this  pandemic  together thank you so much  [Music]  you

